    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1142">

                <pb facs="0945" n="935" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg935"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6336/1–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-19T17:00:00-05:00">January 19, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Embtel 95 Jan 12 rptd Paris 3 London 2. Having in mind current situation
                        Tientsin<anchor n="8" xml:id="d1142-f1"/> and unwillingness British and
                    French join in press statement Dept believes issuance press statement re denial
                    communication facilities ConGen Mukden unwise at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1142-f1" n="8" xml:id="d1142-f1-content">
                <p>Tientsin was occupied by the Chinese Communists on January 15; for documentation
                    regarding problems of the Consulate General at Tientsin after the occupation,
                    see <ref target="#pg1051">pp. 1051</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
